@ ---- LBL :TMAT: X = a colour w (the opponent of the side whose time ran out): X = 1 when w cannot mate by any
@ series of legal moves (the time-out is a draw), else 0. As python-chess's has_insufficient_material(w): a pawn,
@ rook or queen of w: it can; a knight: not when it is w's only piece and the other side has nothing but its king
@ and queens (pawns, knights, bishops, rooks could block its king: a mate with help); bishops only: not when all
@ the bishops on the board stand on one colour and there is no pawn or knight; a bare king: never. The board is
@ scanned once: R32 w's pawns rooks queens, R33 its knights, R34 its bishops, R35 the other side's pawns knights
